{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "00WL", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-sheaves-injective}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:669a25b537eaf82ac7de241b3087d4fbe1e00514515ba77e2ee9c580257077f5", "source_text": "Injective and surjective maps of sheaves", "source_text_hash": "sha256:648970c9c0e08255ee9ab868cf8e8e42e79d80592657f1294387aec8670d3c69", "unit_id": "tag:00WL:title"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "00WL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\varphi : \\mathcal{F}\n\\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\varphi$", "MATH_0004": "$U$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\varphi : \\mathcal{F}(U)\n\\to \\mathcal{G}(U)$", "MATH_0007": "$\\varphi$", "MATH_0008": "$U$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0010": "$s\\in \\mathcal{G}(U)$", "MATH_0011": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0012": "$i$", "MATH_0013": "$s|_{U_i}$", "MATH_0014": "$\\varphi : \\mathcal{F}(U_i) \\to \\mathcal{G}(U_i)$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-sheaves-injective-surjective}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5cf7c9a5fbdbef8a075d860ac27f48c555829acf5763da51438d38f929f5eddc", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4ca01c1791e6025846c940510b9e9b37c96ef150f2528116e21ec266ddfcfc8d", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site, and let <MATH_0002> be a map of sheaves of sets.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> We say that <MATH_0003> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>injective<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if for every object\n<MATH_0004> of <MATH_0005> the map <MATH_0006> is injective.\n<STRUCT_0003> We say that <MATH_0007> is <TEXTITOPEN_0002>surjective<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if for every object\n<MATH_0008> of <MATH_0009> and every section <MATH_0010>\nthere exists a covering <MATH_0011> such that for\nall <MATH_0012> the restriction <MATH_0013> is in the image of\n<MATH_0014>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cdc015fdab40f2192c2c80cbf4f089c0bd83251ff6120ca3ec4cca2500063d83", "unit_id": "tag:00WM:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "00WL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})$", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "SPACE_0002": "\\ "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-mono-epi-sheaves}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2b0ef31a1e60cc7b94591ff5e077791e3119bb2277761958ab8f35550557bf7d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:17df46707fe8a8cbece687ecb558aa3badc11d2a9b605538a989f52a8f4499af", "source_text": "The injective (resp.<SPACE_0001>surjective) maps defined above\nare exactly the monomorphisms (resp.<SPACE_0002>epimorphisms) of\nthe category <MATH_0001>. A map of sheaves\nis an isomorphism if and only if it is both injective\nand surjective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6ec6c211f62ce304001b07cba29e29ee87d12c1ce41a34baa05a72835b161084", "unit_id": "tag:00WN:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "00WL", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ab0671cebd46077100b1c3d49f467867803131b3a6d27bcb6541f0249253a651", "source_text": "Omitted.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:872a8cfa74892c6e6464bd864d9f1c292f4f523caba3e51ac3dafbfc84db48f6", "unit_id": "tag:00WN:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "00WL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{F} \\times_\\mathcal{G} \\mathcal{F}\n\\ar@<1ex>[r] \\ar@<-1ex>[r]\n&\n\\mathcal{F} \\ar[r]\n&\n\\mathcal{G}}\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{G}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-coequalizer-surjection}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ed49a6a8b9116d60f564a40f419df9d3bd5120b8133e6b3866bbd1ef0ea69ed2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a3b098bf5be908044700c7aac59baad94b64f0e4750617c0b4e4428e7d27b3b6", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site. Let <MATH_0002>\nbe a surjection of sheaves of sets. Then the diagram\n<MATH_0003>\nrepresents <MATH_0004> as a coequalizer.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:88b7d43090418eee5e743c93265c7c2bc9dd04ab55302246360ec95549c11ad3", "unit_id": "tag:086K:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "00WL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{H}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\varphi : \\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{H}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F} \\times_\\mathcal{G} \\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{G}' \\subset \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{F} \\times_\\mathcal{G} \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F} \\times_{\\mathcal{G}'} \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\varphi$", "MATH_0009": "$\\psi' : \\mathcal{G}' \\to \\mathcal{H}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{G}'$", "MATH_0012": "$\\psi'$", "MATH_0013": "$\\psi : \\mathcal{G} \\to \\mathcal{H}$", "MATH_0014": "$\\varphi$", "MATH_0015": "$\\psi$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-mono-epi-sheaves}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:535fd16dedd6e75d1c5bdb55442f376b86868fdb8717a2b11dfd71b67d52666e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2e47fa7106b058953ec650e70c5f2fa1911121f8756312bf172650bbeeb681ab", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a sheaf of sets and let\n<MATH_0002> be a map of sheaves equalizing\nthe two maps <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be the presheaf image of\nthe map <MATH_0005>. As the product\n<MATH_0006> may be computed in the\ncategory of presheaves we see that it is equal to the presheaf product\n<MATH_0007>. Hence <MATH_0008>\ninduces a unique map of presheaves <MATH_0009>.\nSince <MATH_0010> is the sheafification of <MATH_0011> by\nLemma <REF_0001>\nwe conclude that <MATH_0012> extends uniquely to a map of sheaves\n<MATH_0013>. We omit the verification that\n<MATH_0014> is equal to the composition of <MATH_0015> and the given map.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:647458ccce402a124d552cd41654779a593aecf36ac0c021997d3f7618e86e41", "unit_id": "tag:086K:proof"}
